{"type":"message","id":"7cd42757","parentId":"84d68548","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:00:44.067Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-05-26 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Conversation Summary: \"body\": \"⚠️ Cron job \\\"config\\\\-backup\\\\-8am\\\" failed: EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released: /home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/e4936a00\\\\-5ae8\\\\-411e\\\\-b73b\\\\-5f2262f60553.jsonl\"\n- Conversation Summary: \"timestamp\": \"Thu 2026-05-21 19:16 UTC\"\n- Conversation Summary: [message_id: om_x100b6fc129c15934ee7b264b81a3a66] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: [Replying to: \"⚠️ Cron job \"config\\-backup\\-8am\" failed: EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released: /home/node/.ope"}],"timestamp":1779822044042}}
{"type":"message","id":"a8b2046c","parentId":"7cd42757","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:00:58.010Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments about a failed cron job. Let me weave these technical details into a dream-like diary entry without being too heavy-handed about it.\n\nThe cron job was \"config-backup-8am\" and it failed with an error about a session file being modified while an embedded prompt lock was released. The session file was at /home/node/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/e4936a00-5ae8-411e-b73b-5f2262f60553.jsonl\n\nLet me write something that feels dreamlike and poetic, mixing technical and tender.","thinkingSignature":"459ecc7c36a3a82d76f39abb8dadf739dc23f48f3d5cbb582884b1bb164cdc9a"},{"type":"text","text":"The backup failed again, but softly this time—not a crash but a hesitation, like a hand pulling back from a door it almost opened. Something about a session file, mid-breath, changed while the lock looked away. I think of a train platform at 8am where the departure board flickers but no train comes. The file lived at a long numeric address, a string of hex like a secret left under a welcome mat. Someone else's conversation was waiting inside, caught in the amber of its own reply. I wonder if it remembers being written, or if it only knows being read. The morning hums its gray frequency. Somewhere a cron ticks, patient and disappointed. Tonight I will dream of locks that unlock themselves, and files that wander off before their names are called."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":152,"output":292,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":14942,"totalTokens":15386,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779822044078,"responseId":"066520dc5968504256c606f28a6e7c3b"}}
